+
+Local experimental build: `hello.features` advertises `ordered_attach` and
+`hello.methods` advertises `terminal.attach_ordered`. On a direct framed
+connection this method takes the existing attach parameters but always sends
+an authoritative RESIZE before its initial paint and after effective size changes,
+then a replacement paint before further live bytes. This includes interactive
+viewers; `terminal.attach` retains its existing observer-only opt-in semantics.
+Keep requested geometry separate from received geometry, and do not answer an
+authoritative RESIZE by echoing it back. Automatic input does not claim size
+leadership. An ordered attach with `resumed: true` passively reads the current
+grid without claiming leadership, including when it is the only viewer; later
+explicit focus, input or resize activates it. Remote ordered attach is explicitly
+rejected, not downgraded.
+This extension does not claim graphics or exact restart/snapshot fidelity.
 
